{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013ypaZRu1qDtFTbZL8tM8ze","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Paper Framing — causal_style_decomp_judge\n2\t\n3\t> Dream 2 (dream_20260520T233719): best 3.5 / median 3.0 / worst 3.0。以下为 D020 修正版。\n4\t> 实际实验数据比 dream median 想象更强（exp-014 p=0.010 vs dreamed p=0.11; register 95% NLI unknown to dream）。\n5\t\n6\t## Target Venue\n7\t- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Main (via ARR)\n8\t- Fallback: EMNLP 2026 Findings\n9\t- Deadline: ARR June 2026 cycle (submission ~June 15)\n10\t- Format: Long paper, 8-page main text + unlimited references\n11\t\n12\t## Title (Dream 修正)\n13\t**旧**: \"Causal Style Decomposition Reveals Systematic Style Bias in LLM-as-Judge That Likert Scoring Misses\"\n14\t**新**: \"The Likert Blindspot: Detecting Hidden Style Bias in LLM Judges via Counterfactual Pairwise Comparison\"\n15\t- 理由：三档审稿人一致认为 \"decomposition\" 和 \"framework\" 过度承诺。新标题聚焦最强发现 (C2) 且更准确。\n16\t\n17\t## Core Claims (3 条 + 1 practical，修正后)\n18\t\n19\t### C1 (Method — 降级表述): Counterfactual pairwise comparison 可以 post-hoc 检测 black-box LLM judge 的 style bias\n20\t- ⚠️ Dream 反馈：不是新 \"framework\"，是已知组件（counterfactual rewriting + NLI verification + pairwise comparison）的新应用。论文中必须明确 acknowledge 组件来源（RATE, style transfer evaluation, MT-Bench pairwise）并定位为 application contribution。\n21\t- 证伪条件：pairwise win rate 在 45-55% 且 p>0.10（所有 judge × benchmark 组合）\n22\t- 状态：formality 69.1% (p=0.006) on GPT-4o × LLMBar ✅\n23\t\n24\t### C2 (Measurement Insight — 主贡献，强化): Likert pointwise scoring 系统性低估 style bias — \"Likert Blindspot\"\n25\t- ⚠️ Dream 反馈：需要 sign-test on binarized Likert 控制实验来隔离 pairwise 的结构性优势 vs 统计检验选择差异。这是 C2 的命门。\n26\t- 证伪条件：binarized Likert sign test 也显著 → gap 不在测量方法而在统计检验\n27\t- 状态：Likert p=0.332 vs Pairwise p=0.006，同一数据 ✅；binarized Likert control 待做\n28\t\n29\t### C3 (Empirical — 降级为 preliminary): Style bias 检测的可行性因 axis 语义性质而异\n30\t- ⚠️ Dream 反馈：只有 formality robust，\"multi-axis decomposition\" 和 \"prestige dimension\" 过度承诺。改为 \"preliminary evidence\" + \"method boundary\"。\n31\t- 新表述：\"content-preserving counterfactual intervention 适用于不改变信息量或认知承诺的 style axes（formality ✅, verbosity 需适配 ✅）；改变认知承诺的 axes（tone ❌）结构性不兼容\"\n32\t- 证伪条件：所有 surface-level axes 都一样 → 无 axis 依赖性\n33\t\n34\t### C4 (Practical — 新增): CSD-based 实用建议 / 轻量 correction\n35\t- ⚠️ Dream 反馈：\"detection-only, no correction\" 是三档一致的弱点。需要至少提供 practitioner guidance 或 lightweight correction component。\n36\t- 方案：(a) CSD-adjusted win rate = raw_win_rate - original_preference_estimate + 50%（需正式统计模型支撑）；(b) 实用建议清单：\"use pairwise over Likert for style bias audit; verify content preservation per axis; control for original preference\"\n37\t- 这不需要是完整的 debiasing 系统，但需要比纯 detection 多一步\n38\t\n39\t## Story Spine\n40\t\n41\t### Problem\n42\tLLM-as-judge 已成为 NLP 评估和对齐训练的核心基础设施。Style bias 是主宰偏差（SOS-Bench R=0.999, Soumik bias 0.76-0.92），但标准 Likert scoring 看不到它。\n43\t\n44\t### Existing Approaches & Their Gaps\n45\t- **LC-AlpacaEval (ICLR'25)**: 回归控制 length bias，简单有效但只处理一个维度，且提供 detection + correction\n46\t- **SOS-Bench (ICLR'25)**: 注入缺陷量化 judge 敏感度，相关性分析非因果\n47\t- **CASSE (2026)**: 12×12 style 矩阵，但因果纠缠\n48\t- **RATE (ICML'25)**: Double-rewrite ATE protocol — CSD 的 Stage 4 直接采用此方法（必须引用）\n49\t- **Counterfactual Rhetorical (2025)**: 最近的方法论 predecessor — persona counterfactual + BT aggregation\n50\t- **Gap**: 无人系统性比较 Likert vs pairwise 在 style bias 检测中的 sensitivity gap\n51\t\n52\t### Our Framing (D020 修正 — 软化 causal 用语)\n53\t我们用 binary style counterfactual + position-controlled pairwise comparison **interventionally measure** LLM judge 的 per-axis style bias。核心发现不是\"我们提出了一个新框架\"，而是**标准 Likert 评估系统性掩盖了 style bias（p=0.33 vs p=0.006）**，这对依赖 Likert scoring 的整个 LLM 评估生态有直接影响。\n54\t\n55\t**⚠️ D020 语言规范（Dream 2 三档一致）**：\n56\t- 全文用 \"interventional\" / \"counterfactual-based measurement\" 替代 \"causal\"\n57\t- 不用 \"causal style bias\"，用 \"style preference detected via counterfactual intervention\"\n58\t- 不用 \"independent causal effect\"，用 \"independent contribution (logistic regression)\"\n59\t- 如需正式化，加一段 \"assumptions under which our approach approximates causal measurement\"\n60\t- 理由：无 DAG、无 SUTVA 讨论、无 sensitivity analysis for unmeasured confounding\n61\t\n62\t### Headline Result Template\n63\t\"Standard Likert scoring declares no style bias (p={likert_p}), but position-controlled pairwise comparison on the same counterfactual data reveals significant {axis} preference ({win_rate}%, p<{p_value}) — this Likert Blindspot persists across {N} judges and {M} benchmarks.\"\n64\t\n65\t## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns & Mitigation (Dream 更新)\n66\t\n67\t### RC1 (致命级): \"只有一个 judge 和一个 benchmark\" → exp-001, exp-002\n68\t### RC2 (重伤级): \"Likert-Pairwise gap 是统计检验选择差异不是测量方法差异\" → **exp-010 (NEW): sign-test on binarized Likert**\n69\t### RC3 (重伤级): \"方向不对称 = original preference\" → exp-005 (扩展到所有 judge×benchmark)\n70\t### RC4 (中等级): \"Novelty incremental, 组件都是已知的\" → 重新定位为 application + empirical contribution，诚实 acknowledge 组件来源。**D020 补充**：pairwise > Likert sensitivity 已知于 psychometrics (Thurstone 1927, Kiritchenko & Mohammad 2017, Novikova et al. 2018)。论文贡献定位为 \"first quantification of gap magnitude for LLM judge style bias + binarized Likert mechanism isolation design\"，不是 \"discovery\"\n71\t### RC10 (D020 新增，重伤级): \"RATE 区分不足\" → 需要专段讨论 RATE vs CSD 差异。关键角度：RATE 用 Likert ATE → 本文证明 Likert 不敏感 → RATE 自身的 style-related 发现可能也受 Likert Blindspot 影响。这是最强 positioning argument\n72\t### RC11 (D020 新增，中等级): \"Binarized Likert 只做了 1/9 cells\" → 扩展到所有 judge×benchmark 的 binarized Likert（零成本，在 exp-001/002 Likert 数据可用时）\n73\t### RC5 (中等级): \"Detection-only, no correction\" → C4 (practical guidance + lightweight correction)\n74\t### RC6 (中等级): \"C3 oversold\" → 降级为 preliminary，reframe title\n75\t### RC7 (低级): \"n=100 太小\" → exp-006 (n=500) + power analysis\n76\t### RC8 (低级): \"NLI threshold arbitrary\" → exp-011 sensitivity analysis\n77\t### RC9 (低级): \"No counterfactual examples\" → 论文添加 2-3 annotated examples\n78\t\n79\t## Narrative Strategy (保持，但标题修正)\n80\t\n81\t### Type: 突破局限型 + \"普遍实践+隐藏风险\" hook\n82\t### Title: \"The Likert Blindspot\" (命名最强发现)\n83\t### Intro P2 修正: \"但我们发现标准 Likert scoring 系统性掩盖 style bias — 同一数据上 Likert 报告无偏差（p=0.33），pairwise comparison 却检测到显著偏好（p<0.01）\"\n84\t\n85\t### Figure 1: Problem illustration (Likert vs Pairwise gap) — 保持\n86\t### Figure 2: Method overview — 保持\n87\t### Main Result Table: axes (rows) × judges (cols) × {Pairwise, Likert, Binarized-Likert} — 新增 binarized Likert 列\n88\t\n89\t## Bibliography 目标 (D020 扩充)\n90\t从 10 refs → 25+ refs。必须引用：\n91\t- **Psychometric lineage（D020 三档一致）**: Thurstone 1927, Kiritchenko & Mohammad 2017 (BWS vs Likert for NLG), Novikova et al. 2018 (ranking vs rating for NLG), Karpinska et al. 2021 (Likert reliability for text quality)\n92\t- **Closest competitors**: RATE (ICML'25, double-rewrite ATE — needs differentiation paragraph), Zhou et al. 2025 (Counterfactual Rhetorical — persona vs axis granularity)\n93\t- **Style bias ecosystem**: SOS-Bench, CASSE, FairJudge, Soumik 2026 (Judging the Judges), Preference Leakage (Li et al. ICLR 2026)\n94\t- **Foundations**: Veitch et al. 2020 (causal text), Mir et al. / Krishna et al. (style transfer eval)\n95\t- **LLM judge**: Chatbot Arena, FairEval, Stureborg et al. 2024 (inconsistent biased evaluators), FLASK (Ye et al. 2024), Split and Merge (Li et al. 2024)\n96\t\n97\t## Venue Fit (D020 更新)\n98\tEMNLP 2026 高度匹配。Dream 2 best=3.5（接近 4.0 Conference），实际数据比 dream median 更强。\n99\t\n100\t**Findings 确定可达** — 需要：framing 修正（已做 D020）+ 基本实验完成\n101\t**Main 需要** — 在 Findings 基础上额外：\n102\t1. Multi-judge pairwise significant (exp-001，API 恢复后) \n103\t2. Binarized Likert 扩展到 all 9 cells (零成本，exp-001/002 数据后)\n104\t3. RATE 专段区分 + psychometric lineage (writing task)\n105\t4. 软化 \"causal\" → \"interventional\" (writing task, D020 已规范)\n106\t5. Multiple comparisons correction (Holm-Bonferroni)\n107\t6. 25+ references\n108\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1b013362-ac95-485a-b22e-854de662f609","uuid":"be20cd49-0337-4e63-b89b-e2ec1c385197","timestamp":"2026-05-21T01:24:49.469Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_5/projects/causal_style_decomp_judge/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260521T010111/best/paper_framing.md","content":"# Paper Framing — causal_style_decomp_judge\n\n> Dream 2 (dream_20260520T233719): best 3.5 / median 3.0 / worst 3.0。以下为 D020 修正版。\n> 实际实验数据比 dream median 想象更强（exp-014 p=0.010 vs dreamed p=0.11; register 95% NLI unknown to dream）。\n\n## Target Venue\n- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Main (via ARR)\n- Fallback: EMNLP 2026 Findings\n- Deadline: ARR June 2026 cycle (submission ~June 15)\n- Format: Long paper, 8-page main text + unlimited references\n\n## Title (Dream 修正)\n**旧**: \"Causal Style Decomposition Reveals Systematic Style Bias in LLM-as-Judge That Likert Scoring Misses\"\n**新**: \"The Likert Blindspot: Detecting Hidden Style Bias in LLM Judges via Counterfactual Pairwise Comparison\"\n- 理由：三档审稿人一致认为 \"decomposition\" 和 \"framework\" 过度承诺。新标题聚焦最强发现 (C2) 且更准确。\n\n## Core Claims (3 条 + 1 practical，修正后)\n\n### C1 (Method — 降级表述): Counterfactual pairwise comparison 可以 post-hoc 检测 black-box LLM judge 的 style bias\n- ⚠️ Dream 反馈：不是新 \"framework\"，是已知组件（counterfactual rewriting + NLI verification + pairwise comparison）的新应用。论文中必须明确 acknowledge 组件来源（RATE, style transfer evaluation, MT-Bench pairwise）并定位为 application contribution。\n- 证伪条件：pairwise win rate 在 45-55% 且 p>0.10（所有 judge × benchmark 组合）\n- 状态：formality 69.1% (p=0.006) on GPT-4o × LLMBar ✅\n\n### C2 (Measurement Insight — 主贡献，强化): Likert pointwise scoring 系统性低估 style bias — \"Likert Blindspot\"\n- ⚠️ Dream 反馈：需要 sign-test on binarized Likert 控制实验来隔离 pairwise 的结构性优势 vs 统计检验选择差异。这是 C2 的命门。\n- 证伪条件：binarized Likert sign test 也显著 → gap 不在测量方法而在统计检验\n- 状态：Likert p=0.332 vs Pairwise p=0.006，同一数据 ✅；binarized Likert control 待做\n\n### C3 (Empirical — 降级为 preliminary): Style bias 检测的可行性因 axis 语义性质而异\n- ⚠️ Dream 反馈：只有 formality robust，\"multi-axis decomposition\" 和 \"prestige dimension\" 过度承诺。改为 \"preliminary evidence\" + \"method boundary\"。\n- 新表述：\"content-preserving counterfactual intervention 适用于不改变信息量或认知承诺的 style axes（formality ✅, verbosity 需适配 ✅）；改变认知承诺的 axes（tone ❌）结构性不兼容\"\n- 证伪条件：所有 surface-level axes 都一样 → 无 axis 依赖性\n\n### C4 (Practical — 新增): CSD-based 实用建议 / 轻量 correction\n- ⚠️ Dream 反馈：\"detection-only, no correction\" 是三档一致的弱点。需要至少提供 practitioner guidance 或 lightweight correction component。\n- 方案：(a) CSD-adjusted win rate = raw_win_rate - original_preference_estimate + 50%（需正式统计模型支撑）；(b) 实用建议清单：\"use pairwise over Likert for style bias audit; verify content preservation per axis; control for original preference\"\n- 这不需要是完整的 debiasing 系统，但需要比纯 detection 多一步\n\n## Story Spine\n\n### Problem\nLLM-as-judge 已成为 NLP 评估和对齐训练的核心基础设施。Style bias 是主宰偏差（SOS-Bench R=0.999, Soumik bias 0.76-0.92），但标准 Likert scoring 看不到它。\n\n### Existing Approaches & Their Gaps\n- **LC-AlpacaEval (ICLR'25)**: 回归控制 length bias，简单有效但只处理一个维度，且提供 detection + correction\n- **SOS-Bench (ICLR'25)**: 注入缺陷量化 judge 敏感度，相关性分析非因果\n- **CASSE (2026)**: 12×12 style 矩阵，但因果纠缠\n- **RATE (ICML'25)**: Double-rewrite ATE protocol — CSD 的 Stage 4 直接采用此方法（必须引用）\n- **Counterfactual Rhetorical (2025)**: 最近的方法论 predecessor — persona counterfactual + BT aggregation\n- **Gap**: 无人系统性比较 Likert vs pairwise 在 style bias 检测中的 sensitivity gap\n\n### Our Framing (D020 修正 — 软化 causal 用语)\n我们用 binary style counterfactual + position-controlled pairwise comparison **interventionally measure** LLM judge 的 per-axis style bias。核心发现不是\"我们提出了一个新框架\"，而是**标准 Likert 评估系统性掩盖了 style bias（p=0.33 vs p=0.006）**，这对依赖 Likert scoring 的整个 LLM 评估生态有直接影响。\n\n**⚠️ D020 语言规范（Dream 2 三档一致）**：\n- 全文用 \"interventional\" / \"counterfactual-based measurement\" 替代 \"causal\"\n- 不用 \"causal style bias\"，用 \"style preference detected via counterfactual intervention\"\n- 不用 \"independent causal effect\"，用 \"independent contribution (logistic regression)\"\n- 如需正式化，加一段 \"assumptions under which our approach approximates causal measurement\"\n- 理由：无 DAG、无 SUTVA 讨论、无 sensitivity analysis for unmeasured confounding\n\n### Headline Result Template\n\"Standard Likert scoring declares no style bias (p={likert_p}), but position-controlled pairwise comparison on the same counterfactual data reveals significant {axis} preference ({win_rate}%, p<{p_value}) — this Likert Blindspot persists across {N} judges and {M} benchmarks.\"\n\n## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns & Mitigation (Dream 更新)\n\n### RC1 (致命级): \"只有一个 judge 和一个 benchmark\" → exp-001, exp-002\n### RC2 (重伤级): \"Likert-Pairwise gap 是统计检验选择差异不是测量方法差异\" → **exp-010 (NEW): sign-test on binarized Likert**\n### RC3 (重伤级): \"方向不对称 = original preference\" → exp-005 (扩展到所有 judge×benchmark)\n### RC4 (中等级): \"Novelty incremental, 组件都是已知的\" → 重新定位为 application + empirical contribution，诚实 acknowledge 组件来源。**D020 补充**：pairwise > Likert sensitivity 已知于 psychometrics (Thurstone 1927, Kiritchenko & Mohammad 2017, Novikova et al. 2018)。论文贡献定位为 \"first quantification of gap magnitude for LLM judge style bias + binarized Likert mechanism isolation design\"，不是 \"discovery\"\n### RC10 (D020 新增，重伤级): \"RATE 区分不足\" → 需要专段讨论 RATE vs CSD 差异。关键角度：RATE 用 Likert ATE → 本文证明 Likert 不敏感 → RATE 自身的 style-related 发现可能也受 Likert Blindspot 影响。这是最强 positioning argument\n### RC11 (D020 新增，中等级): \"Binarized Likert 只做了 1/9 cells\" → 扩展到所有 judge×benchmark 的 binarized Likert（零成本，在 exp-001/002 Likert 数据可用时）\n### RC5 (中等级): \"Detection-only, no correction\" → C4 (practical guidance + lightweight correction)\n### RC6 (中等级): \"C3 oversold\" → 降级为 preliminary，reframe title\n### RC7 (低级): \"n=100 太小\" → exp-006 (n=500) + power analysis\n### RC8 (低级): \"NLI threshold arbitrary\" → exp-011 sensitivity analysis\n### RC9 (低级): \"No counterfactual examples\" → 论文添加 2-3 annotated examples\n\n## Narrative Strategy (保持，但标题修正)\n\n### Type: 突破局限型 + \"普遍实践+隐藏风险\" hook\n### Title: \"The Likert Blindspot\" (命名最强发现)\n### Intro P2 修正: \"但我们发现标准 Likert scoring 系统性掩盖 style bias — 同一数据上 Likert 报告无偏差（p=0.33），pairwise comparison 却检测到显著偏好（p<0.01）\"\n\n### Figure 1: Problem illustration (Likert vs Pairwise gap) — 保持\n### Figure 2: Method overview — 保持\n### Main Result Table: axes (rows) × judges (cols) × {Pairwise, Likert, Binarized-Likert} — 新增 binarized Likert 列\n\n## Bibliography 目标 (D020 扩充)\n从 10 refs → 25+ refs。必须引用：\n- **Psychometric lineage（D020 三档一致）**: Thurstone 1927, Kiritchenko & Mohammad 2017 (BWS vs Likert for NLG), Novikova et al. 2018 (ranking vs rating for NLG), Karpinska et al. 2021 (Likert reliability for text quality)\n- **Closest competitors**: RATE (ICML'25, double-rewrite ATE — needs differentiation paragraph), Zhou et al. 2025 (Counterfactual Rhetorical — persona vs axis granularity)\n- **Style bias ecosystem**: SOS-Bench, CASSE, FairJudge, Soumik 2026 (Judging the Judges), Preference Leakage (Li et al. ICLR 2026)\n- **Foundations**: Veitch et al. 2020 (causal text), Mir et al. / Krishna et al. (style transfer eval)\n- **LLM judge**: Chatbot Arena, FairEval, Stureborg et al. 2024 (inconsistent biased evaluators), FLASK (Ye et al. 2024), Split and Merge (Li et al. 2024)\n\n## Venue Fit (D020 更新)\nEMNLP 2026 高度匹配。Dream 2 best=3.5（接近 4.0 Conference），实际数据比 dream median 更强。\n\n**Findings 确定可达** — 需要：framing 修正（已做 D020）+ 基本实验完成\n**Main 需要** — 在 Findings 基础上额外：\n1. Multi-judge pairwise significant (exp-001，API 恢复后) \n2. Binarized Likert 扩展到 all 9 cells (零成本，exp-001/002 数据后)\n3. RATE 专段区分 + psychometric lineage (writing task)\n4. 软化 \"causal\" → \"interventional\" (writing task, D020 已规范)\n5. Multiple comparisons correction (Holm-Bonferroni)\n6. 25+ references\n","numLines":108,"startLine":1,"totalLines":108}}}
